====================================================================================================
agentY_quasistatic.py -- lens-only slip sector: quasi-static derivation (sympy)
====================================================================================================

[SA] TENSOR SECTOR: c_T and alpha_M on a TT-perturbed background (unitary gauge T=t, N=1)
  S_slip on TT background contains derivatives of h_ij : False
  => the slip sector contributes ZERO to the tensor kinetic structure:
     c_T^2 = 1 IDENTICALLY (all backgrounds, incl. inside halos where Y != 0)   [GW170817: exact pass]
     alpha_M = 0 IDENTICALLY (tensor kinetic coefficient = M_P^2/2, untouched)  [GW friction: exact pass]
  residual h-coupling (algebraic, the standard minimal-coupling source):
    (2*hc(t, z)*Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), x)*Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), y) + hp(t, z)*Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), x)**2 - hp(t, z)*Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), y)**2)*Subs(Derivative(J(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, (Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), x)**2 + Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), y)**2 + Derivative(chibar(x, y, z), z)**2)/a0**2)
  -> a SOURCE term (chi-stress sourcing curvature), not a propagation modification;
     identical in kind to any minimally coupled scalar in GR. Quantified vs GW bounds in agentY_gates.py SE.

[SB] FRW QUIETNESS: the khronon is comoving on FRW => a_mu = 0 => the source coupling is OFF
  FRW khronon acceleration a_mu = [0, 0, 0, 0]  (identically zero)
  => chi-source = 0; with J(0)=0, J'(0) finite: chi = const, Y = 0, T^slip_munu = 0 on FRW.
  => NO cosmological scalar background: the GW->scalar decay channel (1809.03484-class, the
     |alpha_H| <~ 1e-10 kill of cosmological DHOST slip) has no medium to decay into. Evaded by design.
  => alpha_H-equivalent on FRW = 0 ; the sector wakes only where a_mu != 0 (halos), keyed to g_bar.

[SC] STATIC SPHERICAL QUASI-STATIC SYSTEM (the heart)
  (3)R O(e) part: 4*(-r**2*Derivative(Mf(r), (r, 2)) + r*(Derivative(Lf(r), r) - 3*Derivative(Mf(r), r)) + Lf(r) - Mf(r))/r**2    [= -4 Mf'' - 8 Mf'/r + (4/r^2)(Lf - Mf) + 2(Lf' - Mf')... structure check by GR gate below]
  O(eps^2) Lagrangian assembled (all operators at one order: MOND-homogeneous).
  dPhi-eq has 3rd/4th derivatives: True
  dL-eq has 3rd/4th derivatives: False
  dM-eq has 3rd/4th derivatives: False
  dchi-eq has 3rd/4th derivatives: True

  GR GATE (slip off): the four equations in the isotropic gauge:
    dPhi(N):  r*(-4*pi*G*r*rhob(r) + 2*Psi1 + Psi2*r)/(4*pi*G)
    dL(rr):  r*(-Phi1 + Psi1)/(4*pi*G)
    dM(tang):  r*(-Phi1 - Phi2*r + Psi1 + Psi2*r)/(4*pi*G)
    [expect: dPhi => lap Psi = 4 pi G rhob ; dL = radial constraint (1st order);
     dM => combination giving Phi=Psi on shell]

  SOLVING: exact in {J,S,K,F,w}; first order in {C1,C2,C3}:

  PROFILE EQUATION (first integral; C off):
    P/r^2 = -2*J1*chi1 + Phi1   x 1/(8 pi G)
    => sigma Phi' = 2 J'(Y) chi' / (S + 2 Y S')   [the AQUAL-form source relation]
    branch: [2*J1*chi1]

  THE rr-CONSTRAINT:
    C=0 part on-shell: r*(-Phi1 + Psi1)/(4*pi*G)    [= r(Psi'-Phi')/(4 pi G): zero slip without C]

  THE SLIP (algebraic, from the constraint), fully on-shell:  Psi' - Phi' =
     -8*J1**2*alpha**4*c10*chi1**3 + 16*J1**2*alpha**4*c20*chi1**3 + 16*J1**2*alpha**2*c21*chi1**5 - 8*J1**2*alpha**2*c30*chi1**5 + 48*J1*J2*alpha**2*c20*chi1**5 + 32*J1*J2*c21*chi1**7 + 2*J1*alpha**4*c10*chi1**3 - 4*J1*alpha**4*c20*chi1**3 - 4*J1*alpha**2*c21*chi1**5 + 2*J1*alpha**2*c30*chi1**5 - 4*J2*alpha**2*c10*chi1**5 - 4*J2*alpha**2*c20*chi1**5 - 4*J2*c30*chi1**7 + (-16*pi*G*J2*alpha**2*c10*chi1**4*r - 16*pi*G*J2*alpha**2*c20*chi1**4*r - 16*pi*G*J2*c30*chi1**6*r)*rhob(r)   / [ 4*J1*alpha**6 + 8*J2*alpha**4*chi1**2 - alpha**6 ]

